\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Cross-sectional visualisations of the breeder blanket layers illustrating the effect of the linear gradient parameter, $\zeta $. This parameter controls the radial distribution of layer thicknesses: (a) a forward-weighted geometry shifting volume towards the first wall, (b) the baseline uniform thickness distribution, and (c) a rear-weighted geometry shifting volume deeper into the blanket.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
