\newlabel{fig:zeta_parameter}{{1}{2}{Cross-sectional visualisations of the breeder blanket layers illustrating the effect of the linear gradient parameter, $\zeta $. This parameter controls the radial distribution of layer thicknesses: (a) a forward-weighted geometry shifting volume towards the first wall, (b) the baseline uniform thickness distribution, and (c) a rear-weighted geometry shifting volume deeper into the blanket}{figure.caption.1}{}}
